<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    Mach-O __eh_frame function starts (`option machoehframe on|off`, default on).

    A Mach-O falls back to a DWARF FDE in __TEXT,__eh_frame for a function its
    compact unwind encoding cannot describe. Every FDE pcBegin is a function
    start, as on ELF, where kuna reads .eh_frame in its always-on entry
    discovery; until this option, the Mach-O __eh_frame was never read.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 code-data-partition, the Mach-O entry-discovery
    oracles (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/entry/kuna_machoehframe.rs`),
    committed at `read symbols`.

    P0 assertion: `option machoehframe on|off`, set after `load file` and
    before the `read symbols` that commits the discovered entries.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes load
    the arm64 Mach-O fixture `macho_ehframe_only_arm64` (built from
    `macho_ehframe_only_arm64.s`): LC_FUNCTION_STARTS and the local symbols are
    stripped, and three uncalled eh_* functions are recorded only by their
    __eh_frame FDEs (and by __unwind_info, which `unwindstarts` reads and
    leaves off by default).

    Pass 1 (`option machoehframe off`, the BUG): `functions` lists only _main.
    Pass 2 (the default, the FIX): the three FDE starts are listed, and one of
    them decompiles as a function.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_ehframe_only_arm64</com>
  <com>option machoehframe off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_ehframe_only_arm64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>load function sub_100000378</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="machoehframe: both passes discover the LC_MAIN entry" min="2" max="2">0x10000040c _main</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="machoehframe: the first FDE start joins the inventory (off: absent)" min="1" max="1">0x100000330 sub_100000330</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="machoehframe: the second FDE start joins the inventory (off: absent)" min="1" max="1">0x100000378 sub_100000378</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="machoehframe: the third FDE start joins the inventory (off: absent)" min="1" max="1">0x1000003c0 sub_1000003c0</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="machoehframe: a recovered start decompiles as a function" min="1" max="1">sub_100000378\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
